course: dictionary
lesson: 8090
title: Remembrance: keeping people in mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Remembrance means the act of remembering someone or something, especially people who have died. Its root is remember, so if you have remembrance for someone, you keep them in your thoughts. «Remembrance Day on 11 November marks the end of the First World War in 1918, and people wear red poppies.» Remembrance Day is a day for keeping the soldiers in mind.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A minute's silence in remembrance» and «people stand still and silent to remember the soldiers who died in wars» both show quiet, serious thinking about people who have died. The silence and standing still tell you the word is about remembering with respect.
explain: Remembrance has a second meaning: something that helps you remember, like a gift or a memorial. A red poppy can be a remembrance because it reminds people of the soldiers. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «Many people wear a red poppy as a remembrance» still makes sense when you think of a thing that helps you remember.
fact: Remembrance means remembering, especially people who have died.
fact: «Remembrance Day» on 11 November honours soldiers who died in wars.
fact: On Remembrance Day many people observe a two-minute silence and wear a red poppy.
fact: Remembrance Sunday is the UK name for this day, Anzac Day is used in Australia and New Zealand, and Veterans Day is used in the USA.
fact: Remembrance is usually a noun with no plural, so write «remembrance», not «remembrances».
exercise: «The town held a two-minute silence in remembrance of the soldiers.» What does remembrance mean here? | A new shop opening on the high street | *Keeping the soldiers in our minds with respect | A loud party with music and dancing
exercise: «Many people wear a red poppy as a remembrance.» What does remembrance mean in this sentence? | A football match | A map of the town | *A thing that helps you remember | A loud noise in the street
exercise: «Remembrance Day, 11 November, honours those who died in wars.» Find and copy the month of Remembrance Day. | March | *November | April | July
test: What does remembrance mean? | *Keeping in mind someone who has died | To forget something on purpose | A type of cake | A loud game played outside
test: In the USA, which day is like Remembrance Day? | Christmas Day | Independence Day | *Veterans Day | Halloween
exam: Which sentence uses remembrance to mean something that helps you remember? | We went to remembrance on Sunday for a picnic | Remembrance Day is the day after Monday | The team had a long remembrance of the match | *The ticket is a remembrance of our trip to the coast
